; DEVS:NetInterfaces/wifipi -- written by the AmiNetXDuo installer.
;
; The name of this file is the name of the interface.  Use it
; with the network commands:
;
;     Online eth0
;     Offline eth0
;     ShowNetStatus INTERFACE eth0
;
; DEVICE     the SANA-II driver for the card.  A bare name is
;            looked up in DEVS:.  A path is used as given.
; UNIT       which card, when one driver has several.
; CONFIGURE  how the address is obtained:
;              DHCP   -- ask the network (the usual choice)
;              AUTO   -- self-assign 169.254.x.x with no DHCP
;              STATIC -- use the ADDRESS/NETMASK below
;              NONE   -- no IPv4 here, IPv6 carries this
;                        interface
;            Note this keyword is CONFIGURE, not IPTYPE.  In
;            Roadshow IPTYPE is the SANA-II packet type, a
;            number, and defaults to 2048.
;
; MDNS=  YES -- answer .local queries on this interface
;        NO  -- do not, which is the default when the
;               keyword is absent.  The responder costs
;               real time on a slow machine, even when
;               nothing asks it anything.
;
; An IPv6 build also understands CONFIGURE6 (OFF, LINKLOCAL,
; AUTO, DHCP or STATIC), ADDRESS6 and GATEWAY6.  A build
; without IPv6 ignores them, so they are safe to leave in
; place.  AUTO follows the router, which is what an IPv6-only
; machine behind a managed router needs; see
; Examples/NetInterfaces/eth0-ipv6.
;
DEVICE=DEVS:Networks/wifipi.device
UNIT=0
CONFIGURE=DHCP
MDNS=YES
;ADDRESS=192.168.1.10
;NETMASK=255.255.255.0
;CONFIGURE6=AUTO
